1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,084
Your head is older than
your feet.

2
00:00:02,384 --> 00:00:04,144
Every second you're
standing,

3
00:00:04,144 --> 00:00:06,139
it pulls a tiny bit
further ahead.

4
00:00:06,539 --> 00:00:07,629
Here's the thing.

5
00:00:07,629 --> 00:00:09,547
Gravity doesn't just
pull on you.

6
00:00:09,547 --> 00:00:10,959
It slows down time.

7
00:00:11,409 --> 00:00:13,045
The closer you are to
Earth,

8
00:00:13,045 --> 00:00:14,626
the slower your clock
ticks.

9
00:00:14,876 --> 00:00:16,304
Your feet are closer.

10
00:00:16,304 --> 00:00:17,625
Your head is higher.

11
00:00:17,625 --> 00:00:19,869
So your head's time runs
a little faster.

12
00:00:20,369 --> 00:00:21,520
Sounds made up.

13
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,497
So in 2010,

14
00:00:22,497 --> 00:00:26,325
physicists at a U.S. lab
called NIST tested it.

15
00:00:26,675 --> 00:00:27,542
They took two

16
00:00:27,542 --> 00:00:29,339
super-precise atomic
clocks,

17
00:00:29,339 --> 00:00:31,400
and raised one by about
a foot.

18
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,944
Two steps up a
staircase.

19
00:00:33,144 --> 00:00:34,855
The higher clock ticked
faster.

20
00:00:35,005 --> 00:00:37,296
Over a whole
seventy-nine year life,

21
00:00:37,296 --> 00:00:39,278
those two steps add up
to about

22
00:00:39,278 --> 00:00:41,136
ninety billionths of a
second.

23
00:00:41,536 --> 00:00:43,129
Far too small to feel.

24
00:00:43,129 --> 00:00:43,930
But real.

25
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:45,875
And your phone feels it.

26
00:00:45,875 --> 00:00:47,864
GPS satellites fly high,

27
00:00:47,864 --> 00:00:49,852
so their clocks run
fast.

28
00:00:50,052 --> 00:00:52,698
So engineers set them
slower on the ground,

29
00:00:52,698 --> 00:00:53,680
before launch.

30
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:56,073
Without that fix, your
map would be wrong.

31
00:00:56,373 --> 00:00:57,441
The verdict?

32
00:00:57,441 --> 00:00:58,146
True.

33
00:00:58,146 --> 00:01:00,900
The higher you are, the
faster your time runs.

34
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:04,095
So next time you take
the stairs,

35
00:01:04,095 --> 00:01:06,040
you just aged a little
faster.

36
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,687
Barely.

37
00:01:07,287 --> 00:01:08,932
Which means your head
really

38
00:01:08,932 --> 00:01:10,433
is older than your feet.

39
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:11,302
By a hair.

